cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Khayyam Math, please cite the preprint below."
title: "Khayyam Math: Live Diagram Generation for Educational Mathematics via Hybrid Neuro-Symbolic Reasoning"
authors:
  - family-names: "Kermani Kolankeh"
    given-names: "Arash"
    affiliation: "School of Engineering, Applied Science and Technology, Canadian University Dubai, United Arab Emirates"
    email: arash.kolankeh@cud.ac.ae
version: "0.1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/khayyam-math/khayyam-math"
license: MIT
type: software
abstract: >
  Khayyam Math converts natural-language mathematics prompts into
  deterministic, byte-reproducible figures with synchronised narration.
  The pipeline combines deterministic per-domain templates (Graphviz,
  matplotlib, SymPy plots) with an LLM fallback gated by a SymPy / Z3 /
  Lean math-correctness verifier and a 50-criterion pre-deploy quality
  gate.  See the repository for the architecture overview and the
  benchmark harness.
keywords:
  - educational technology
  - mathematics
  - diagram generation
  - neuro-symbolic
  - deterministic layout
  - figure verification
